{"duration_api_ms":199922,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"026c78d5-90ef-4015-a0c3-8ea90992bcef","total_cost_usd":0.6315722,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78347,"cache_read_input_tokens":290392,"output_tokens":28823,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":13888},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14680,"cache_read_input_tokens":82708,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":7570,"outputTokens":260,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0008870000000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":232,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":28823,"cacheReadInputTokens":290392,"cacheCreationInputTokens":78347,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6306852000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":13888,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":78347,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer\":\"numerical_auditor\",\"paper_id\":\"bicycle-infrastructure-paper\",\"run_status\":\"ok\",\"summary\":\"Most headline numbers reconcile: the pilot funnel (70 → 34 → 5 → 2), the pilot coding split (5 + 8 + 21 = 34), the agreement tables (33/34 = 97%), the project precision split (19 + 10 + 9 + 5 = 43; 19 + 10 = 29), and Table 8 (266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579; all shares recompute to the printed one-decimal values). The 2 of 18 ceremony and 26 non-ceremony split (18 + 26 = 44; 17 + 2 = 19) and the county shares in Figure 4 also check out. Five issues remain. (1) The 'about 6 percent' yield divides 2 distinct openings by 34 articles, while 5 articles are coded relevant. (2) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Table 3 shows the second coder coded it relevant. (3) The Appendix describes a January–April 2024 gap but the text says only the first quarter is missing, and Figure 3 plots Q2 2024. (4) The Table 9 first-type rule conflicts with its own bysykkelstativ example. (5) The 96-article and 44-project totals cannot be shown to be additive. Parser-quality guidance was respected: table values were read from page text, not the mis-columned table CSV/markdown. Figure 1's bar chart and Figure 3/4 were read from page text and images.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"NUM-001\",\"category\":\"denominator / unit mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The pilot yield 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place' divides 2 distinct openings by 34 articles; the paper itself codes 5 articles as relevant to those 2 openings.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"2/34 = 5.9% is arithmetically correct, but the numerator is a count of distinct events (Figure 1: 'Distinct openings that took place 2') while the denominator is a count of articles. Section 3.1.4 states 'Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found' (four Homborsund and one Stod article), and Figure 1 shows 5 articles coded relevant (15% retained). Two of the four Homborsund articles predate the opening, so the number of articles that actually report a completed opening is 3 in the validation coding. The share of articles concerning a completed opening is therefore 3/34 to 5/34 (about 9% to 15%), depending on the definition. The Figure 1 caption's 'Only 2 of 70 search hits' mixes search hits and events in the same way. The low-yield conclusion likely survives, but the stated rate is an event-per-article ratio, not an article share. The paper does not say which unit it means.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Sentence and Figure 1 chart labels (70, 34, 5, 2) read from page text and page image.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Gives 5 relevant articles for 2 openings; 3 remain after excluding pre-opening articles.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"2 is a count of openings; the paper's own count of relevant articles is 5 (or 3 after excluding pre-opening articles).\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"distinct openings\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Numerator in 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)'\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"5\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles coded relevant\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Five relevant articles reported for the two openings (4 Homborsund, 1 Stod)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Both are counts within the same 34-article pilot, but one counts events and the other counts articles. The share of articles concerning a completed opening is 5/34 = 14.7% (3/34 = 8.8% after excluding the two pre-opening Homborsund articles), versus the reported 2/34 = 5.9%.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"The reported 'about 6 percent' article share uses distinct openings (2) as the numerator over articles (34). On the paper's article counts the share is about 9% to 15%.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The authors may intend an event-yield measure (distinct openings per article) and used 'articles' loosely.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State the unit (e.g., 'two distinct openings, reported in 5 of the 34 articles (15%)'), or define the intended yield. Apply the same fix to the Figure 1 caption's 'Only 2 of 70 search hits'.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Restate the yield with matching units: either 'two openings from 34 articles' or an article-level share (5/34, or 3/34 if pre-opening articles are excluded). Say which definition is used and align the Figure 1 caption.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-002\",\"category\":\"internal count inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 and Section 4.1 show the second coder coded the Stord article relevant.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)\",\"text_quote\":\"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"The project in Stord was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 3 has one article coded Not relevant by the pilot coder and Relevant by the second coder; the second coder's relevant total is 4 versus the pilot coder's 3. Section 4.1 says the only disagreement is the Stord municipality article, and Section 4.2 says the same article is the pilot–LLM disagreement. The Stord article is therefore coded relevant by the second coder and by the LLM (2 of 3 runs). It is coded not relevant only by the pilot coder. Footnote 3's statement that both human coders coded it not relevant conflicts with these counts. This affects the 96 and 44 totals, which rely on the LLM-relevant pilot articles.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"The quote continues 'relevant by both human coders (Section 4)' on the next line.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text (Table 3 and Section 4.1)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1\",\"text_quote\":\"Not relevant 1 30 31\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Row 'Not relevant' (pilot coder) shows 1 article coded Relevant by the second coder; column total Relevant = 4. The Stord disagreement is described in the following paragraph. Read from the page text, not the mis-columned table_3.md, per parser guidance.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Stord article coded not relevant by both human coders\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Table 3 shows one article the second coder coded relevant and the pilot coder did not; Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord article.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"human coders coding the Stord article not relevant\",\"sample\":\"Stord article, pilot, 2 human coders\",\"denominator\":\"2 human coders\",\"context\":\"Footnote 3: 'coded as not relevant by both human coders'\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"1\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"human coders coding the Stord article not relevant\",\"sample\":\"Table 3, 34 pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"2 human coders\",\"context\":\"Table 3 cell: pilot coder Not relevant, second coder Relevant = 1 article (the Stord article per Section 4.1)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Same pilot article and the same two human coders; Table 3 and Section 4.1 define the disagreement article as the Stord article.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Footnote 3 implies 2 of 2 human coders coded it not relevant. Table 3 implies 1 of 2 (the second coder coded it relevant).\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The footnote may be stale from an earlier coding round, or may refer to a stricter 'opening' definition that differs from Table 3's relevance coding.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"Reconcile the footnote with Table 3, e.g. 'coded not relevant by the pilot coder'. If a different definition is meant, state it.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Correct footnote 3 or Table 3/Section 4.1 so they agree on how each human coder coded the Stord article, and confirm how this article enters the 96 articles and 44 projects.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-003\",\"category\":\"timing / period inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The text says only the first quarter of 2024 is missing from the listings, but the Appendix and Figure 3 caption say the gap covers January to April 2024, which also touches Q2 2024; Figure 3 plots Q2 2024.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 Analysis / Figure 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Appendix A.1 and the Figure 3 caption state that listings from January to April 2024 are missing, which is 4 months. Figure 3 shows no point for Q1 2024 but plots a Q2 2024 point (about 39%) between the 2023 Q4 and 2025 points. April is part of Q2, so the Q2 2024 share would rest on at most two months (May–June) of listings, while the other quarterly points use three months. The text does not say whether Q2 2024 was computed on partial data or excluded, and the 'first quarter only' statement understates the gap.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 16 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2\",\"text_quote\":\"missing listing text from January to April 2024.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"The figure caption gives the four-month gap. The statement 'The first quarter of 2024 is missing' is in the preceding body paragraph on the same page.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"figure_3.png\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_3.png\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2\",\"text_quote\":null,\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-22f18338a427285653860df1\",\"correspondence\":\"visual\",\"verification_note\":\"Viewed the crop: points end at Q4 2023 and resume at about Q2 2024. A Q2 2024 point is plotted at about 39%. Point positions were read by eye and are approximate.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Only Q1 2024 is missing\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"The caption gap (Jan–Apr) extends one month into Q2 2024, which is plotted.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"4\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"months missing\",\"sample\":\"Listing text data, 2024\",\"denominator\":\"12 months in 2024\",\"context\":\"Gap stated as January to April 2024\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"3\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"months missing (one quarter)\",\"sample\":\"Listing text data, 2024\",\"denominator\":\"12 months in 2024\",\"context\":\"'The first quarter of 2024 is missing' implies January to March\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Same data gap described in the same appendix section and figure. Four months of missing data cannot be confined to one three-month quarter.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"4 missing months versus 3 months in a single quarter, leaving April 2024 unaccounted for in the Q2 2024 point.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The Q2 2024 point may be computed from May–June only, or the April gap may be partial.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State whether Q2 2024 is based on partial-quarter data, and align the text with the January–April gap.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Describe the gap as January–April 2024 consistently. Say how the Q2 2024 point was computed, or drop it if it rests on partial-quarter data.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-004\",\"category\":\"classification rule vs reported shares\",\"finding_summary\":\"The Table 9 rule 'first type in the table' puts 'bysykkelstativ' in Parking & storage (it contains 'stativ'), but the same paragraph counts it as infrastructure, so the Table 8 and Figure 2 category shares for that word are ambiguous.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions\",\"text_quote\":\"given the first type in the table.\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing “bysykkel” (city bike), such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"In Table 9, Parking & storage appears before Infrastructure and contains the word part 'stativ' (rack). Infrastructure contains 'bysykkel'. 'bysykkelstativ' contains both parts, so the stated first-in-table rule gives Parking & storage, whereas the text says Infrastructure. Similarly, 'syklende' contains 'sykle' (Proximity, listed earlier) but is listed under Infrastructure. Figure 2 shows bysykkelstativ at 0.5% and syklende at 0.3% of all listings, and Table 8 category totals (Parking & storage 10.8%, Infrastructure 13.4%, Proximity 10.7%) depend on this assignment. The category on which the Table 8 counts rest cannot be determined from the text. This is a definition conflict, not a verified miscount.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2\",\"text_quote\":\"given the first type in the table.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"The example about 'bysykkelstativ' follows in the same paragraph. The Table 9 rows were read from the page text, not the single-column table_9.md.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 16 text (Figure 2)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":\"bysykkelstativ (city bike station) 0.5%\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Figure 2 bar labels read from page text.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"First-type-in-table rule assigns bysykkelstativ to infrastructure\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"By table order the word would be Parking & storage.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Which category (Parking & storage or Infrastructure) were 'bysykkelstativ' (0.5% of listings) and 'syklende' (0.3%) counted in when producing Table 8's 10.8% and 13.4%?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"0.5\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"percent of all listings\",\"sample\":\"700,579 FINN.no listings, Jan 2020 to Oct 2026\",\"denominator\":\"700,579 listings\",\"context\":\"Figure 2 share of listings containing 'bysykkelstativ'\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.05\",\"scale\":\"percent\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Which classification order was actually implemented\",\"Word-level counts by assigned category\",\"The overlap between listings containing these words and other words in each category, since the type shares are unions of listings\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Reconcile the stated order rule with the stated example (and with 'syklende'). Report which assignment was used, and, if the rule was misdescribed, confirm that Table 8 and Figure 2 reflect the implemented classification.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-005\",\"category\":\"additivity of totals\",\"finding_summary\":\"The 96 article records and 44 projects are described as 92 + 4 and 43 + 1. The retained text does not establish that the pilot and the rounds 2–4 article sets are disjoint, or that the pilot's Homborsund and Stod projects are already among the 43.\",\"issue_type\":\"cannot_verify\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"low\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)\",\"text_quote\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.\",\"precision\":\"partial\"},\"claim_text\":\"The 96 article records comprise 92 articles from rounds 2–4 and four from the pilot, giving 44 unique projects (43 plus Stord).\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"The additivity of 92 + 4 and 43 + 1 depends on whether the pilot articles (searched 2 September to 10 October 2026) overlap with the 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4 (published October 2025 to October 2026), and whether the Homborsund and Stod projects are among the 43. The retained text does not say.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 5 gives 92 relevant articles and 43 projects from rounds 2–4, published October 2025 to October 2026. The pilot window (2 September to 10 October 2026) lies inside that period, and the pilot's four LLM-relevant articles (Table 4: 3 + 1) cover Homborsund, Stod and Stord. Footnote 3 treats only Stord as new, which implies Homborsund and Stod are in the 43 through rounds 2–4 articles. If any pilot article is also among the 3,187 articles, 96 double-counts it. The text does not state whether the rounds are disjoint, and Table 7 reports on 'rounds 1–4'.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote text on page 10.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 8 text (Table 4)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md\",\"page\":8,\"page_label\":\"8\",\"section\":\"4.2\",\"text_quote\":\"The only article they disagree on is the same\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 4 column total of 4 LLM-relevant articles is on this page. Used only to identify the pilot's four LLM-relevant articles.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"96 = 92 + 4 and 44 = 43 + 1\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"cannot_verify\",\"note\":\"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 articles and projects is not documented.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Are the 4 pilot LLM-relevant articles disjoint from the 92 round 2–4 articles, and are the Homborsund and Stod projects among the 43 projects?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"92\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"Rounds 2–4, 3,187 articles\",\"denominator\":\"3,187 articles\",\"context\":\"Relevant articles in rounds 2–4\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Whether rounds 2–4 exclude the pilot's articles\",\"Project-level overlap between the pilot and the 43 projects\",\"Round definitions (round 1 = pilot?)\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State that the rounds are disjoint at article level, or give the de-duplicated count. Say how the pilot's Homborsund and Stod projects map into the 43 projects.\"}],\"notes\":[\"Table CSV/markdown objects were not used as primary evidence, following the parser-quality guidance; table values were read from page text. The Figure 1 chart was read from the page-4 image and text.\",\"Checked and consistent: 70 − 36 duplicates = 34; 34/70 = 48.6% (printed 49%); 5/34 = 14.7% (printed 15%); 5 + 8 + 21 = 34; 6 unclear for too little text + 2 planned = 8; Table 3 and Table 4 margins and 33/34 = 97.1%; 1/34 = 2.9% (printed 3%); Table 6 day 19 + month 10 = 29 and 19 + 10 + 9 + 5 = 43; 14 of 15 counties; ceremony split 18 + 26 = 44 and 17 + 2 = 19 day-dated; Table 8 sums and every share to one decimal (the 9.8% for 'bicycle' is 9.845%); Table 8 type counts exceed 'Any mention' (346,827 vs 266,625), as the table note allows; text county shares in Figure 4 (61, 52, 14, 13, 7) and the 38.1% national share; Figure 3 trend of about 35% to about 44% is about 9 percentage points as stated.\",\"Table 5 road-link lengths (m0–1492 and m0–641) sum to 2,133 m against the reported 2,132 m; this is within rounding of integer reference positions and was not reported. The Geometry registered 4 September vs opening 5 October interval matches 'one month before'.\",\"The statement that between a third and a half of projects contain most of the other Table 7 groups was checked: 6 of 9 groups fall between 33% and 50% of 44 projects (15/44 to 21/44), and Reasons for delay is 4/44 = 9%. The sentence is hedged with 'most', so it was not reported.\",\"External figures (Copenhagen 60 percent, 5 percentage points for the Bergen tunnel, 96 percent accuracy in Bartik et al.) were not verified; they are literature claims outside this role's retained evidence.\",\"No standard errors, regressions or effect sizes appear. Equations (1) and (2) are proposed specifications and contain no numerical results to audit.\"],\"completion\":{\"version\":1,\"state\":\"complete\",\"scope_description\":\"Numerical audit of work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed: all counts, percentages, shares, totals and dates in the main text, Tables 1–9 and Figures 1–4, with appendix definitions read before recomputation.\",\"checks_completed\":[\"Read the parser-quality guidance and used page text and images instead of mis-columned table CSV/markdown\",\"Read the full text of all 18 pages and the main numeric claims in the abstract, introduction, results, conclusion and appendix\",\"Recomputed the pilot funnel, retention percentages, duplicate counts and the 5 + 8 + 21 coding split\",\"Recomputed the Table 3 and Table 4 margins, agreement percentages and 3% internal-consistency rate\",\"Tested adding-up identities: Table 6 precision categories, 44 projects split by ceremony, Table 8 any/no mention total, and the non-additivity of type rows (stated in the table note)\",\"Recomputed every Table 8 share against the 700,579 denominator and compared it with the Figure 2, Figure 3 and Figure 4 values and the text\",\"Checked the percentage-point statement (35% to 44% = 9 points) against Figure 3, and the Figure 4 county shares and dashed national line against the text\",\"Checked the Table 5 NVDB linkage numbers, the date interval and the road-link length sum\",\"Cross-checked the Table 2/Table 7 counts and the 96 and 44 totals against Section 5 and the footnotes\",\"Checked denominators and units in the text's yield statements\"],\"missing_checks\":[],\"evidence_limitations\":[\"The Figure 3 point values were read by eye from the image and are approximate.\",\"The Table 8 type shares are unions of listings and the word-level overlaps are not given, so category sums could not be tested.\",\"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 articles, round definitions, and the implemented classification order are not documented in the retained text.\",\"External literature numbers were not verified.\"]},\"coverage\":[{\"item_id\":\"assigned_remit\",\"source_object_ids\":[],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Systematic pass over the main text, Tables 1–9, Figures 1–4 and the appendix: recomputed counts, percentages, percentage-point differences, adding-up identities and denominators; read the appendix definitions first; compared text claims with displays.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Five issues found (yield denominator, footnote 3 vs Table 3, the 2024 gap period, the Table 9 rule vs example, the 96/44 additivity); the remaining checked numbers reconcile. numbers_in_text.json was not read item by item; the numeric claims were read directly from full_text.md and the page text.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\",\"NUM-002\",\"NUM-003\",\"NUM-004\",\"NUM-005\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Figure 1 funnel values and caption checked against the page-4 text and image: 34/70 = 49%, 5/34 = 15%, 2 distinct openings, 'Only 2 of 70 search hits'.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The retention percentages are correct, but the yield sentence and caption mix events and articles/hits.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Figure 2 word shares compared with the text (about 5 percent for four words) and with Table 8 (sykkel 9.8% = 68,974/700,579), and checked that the 20 listed shares are descending and consistent with the Table 8 type unions.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Values and the top-word text description reconcile. The bysykkelstativ category assignment is ambiguous (NUM-004).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-004\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Figure 3 inspected as an image: start value about 35%, end value about 44%, dip in the second half of 2023, the 2024 gap, and the text's 9-point rise.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The levels and the 9-point rise match the text; the gap period is described inconsistently (Q1 versus January–April). Values were read by eye.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-003\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Figure 4 county values read from the image and page text; compared with text (61, 52, 14, 13, 7; Oslo to Møre og Romsdal range) and the dashed line at about 38%; counted 15 counties.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All text citations round correctly from the plotted values; 15 counties match '14 of 15'.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 1 read from page-5 text; numeric content limited to examples (3 km, 3.5 m, 30 km/h, '4 articles in 2 newspapers'); compared with Table 2 and Section 3.1.4.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Homborsund 'covered by 4 articles' agrees with Table 2 and Section 3.1.4. No other quantitative claims.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 2 read from page-5 text (the table CSV is truncated): article counts 4 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 7 against five relevant articles plus two planned; dates and footnotes against the text.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Counts (4 + 1 relevant; 1 + 1 planned) match Section 3.1.4. Date arithmetic in the footnotes is internally consistent.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 3 cells and margins recomputed (3 + 0 = 3; 1 + 30 = 31; 3 + 1 = 4; 0 + 30 = 30; total 34); agreement (3 + 30)/34 = 97.06%; compared with footnote 3 on the Stord article.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Table arithmetic is correct. Footnote 3 contradicts the table's second-coder coding of the Stord article.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-002\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 4 cells and margins recomputed; agreement 33/34 = 97.06%; compared with the text on the Stord disagreement and the 'same as human–human' claim.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Arithmetic is correct and the same cell counts as Table 3 are consistent with a single shared disagreement article. The 96/44 totals that rely on its four LLM-relevant articles are discussed in NUM-005.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 5 read from page-9 text: road-link lengths 1492 + 641 = 2,133 m vs reported 2,132 m; geometry date 4 September vs opening 5 October ('one month'); municipality and county numbers.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The 1 m difference is within rounding of integer reference positions and is not reported. The one-month statement matches 31 days.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 6 read from page-10 text: 19 + 10 + 9 + 5 = 43 projects; 19 + 10 = 29 day/month; 14 of 15 counties; 92 relevant and 2 unclear within 3,187; 50 outlets versus 236 in the text.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All figures agree with the abstract, introduction, Section 5 and conclusion.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 7 counts read from page-11 text and converted to shares of 44 (location 42/44 = 95%; others 9% to 55%); compared with the 'between a third and a half' sentence and with the 18 + 26 ceremony split.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Most groups lie between a third and a half; the 'most of the other groups' hedge holds and the sentence was not reported as a defect. The 44 base ties to the footnote 3 total, whose additivity is discussed in NUM-005.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 8 read from page-15 text (the CSV splits thousands): 266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579; all eight shares recomputed against 700,579; type rows' non-additivity (346,827 vs 266,625) compared with the table note.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All shares recompute to the printed values; the text's 38 / 13.4 / about 11 percent figures agree. Non-additivity is declared in the table note.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Table 9 word-part lists read from the page-18 text and compared with the first-type-in-table rule, the bysykkelstativ example and the Figure 2 category colours.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The stated order rule conflicts with the stated example, so the category assignment behind Table 8 shares is ambiguous.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-004\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer":"numerical_auditor","paper_id":"bicycle-infrastructure-paper","run_status":"ok","summary":"Most headline numbers reconcile: the pilot funnel (70 → 34 → 5 → 2), the pilot coding split (5 + 8 + 21 = 34), the agreement tables (33/34 = 97%), the project precision split (19 + 10 + 9 + 5 = 43; 19 + 10 = 29), and Table 8 (266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579; all shares recompute to the printed one-decimal values). The 2 of 18 ceremony and 26 non-ceremony split (18 + 26 = 44; 17 + 2 = 19) and the county shares in Figure 4 also check out. Five issues remain. (1) The 'about 6 percent' yield divides 2 distinct openings by 34 articles, while 5 articles are coded relevant. (2) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Table 3 shows the second coder coded it relevant. (3) The Appendix describes a January–April 2024 gap but the text says only the first quarter is missing, and Figure 3 plots Q2 2024. (4) The Table 9 first-type rule conflicts with its own bysykkelstativ example. (5) The 96-article and 44-project totals cannot be shown to be additive. Parser-quality guidance was respected: table values were read from page text, not the mis-columned table CSV/markdown. Figure 1's bar chart and Figure 3/4 were read from page text and images.","findings":[{"id":"NUM-001","category":"denominator / unit mismatch","finding_summary":"The pilot yield 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place' divides 2 distinct openings by 34 articles; the paper itself codes 5 articles as relevant to those 2 openings.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Pilot sample","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"2/34 = 5.9% is arithmetically correct, but the numerator is a count of distinct events (Figure 1: 'Distinct openings that took place 2') while the denominator is a count of articles. Section 3.1.4 states 'Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found' (four Homborsund and one Stod article), and Figure 1 shows 5 articles coded relevant (15% retained). Two of the four Homborsund articles predate the opening, so the number of articles that actually report a completed opening is 3 in the validation coding. The share of articles concerning a completed opening is therefore 3/34 to 5/34 (about 9% to 15%), depending on the definition. The Figure 1 caption's 'Only 2 of 70 search hits' mixes search hits and events in the same way. The low-yield conclusion likely survives, but the stated rate is an event-per-article ratio, not an article share. The paper does not say which unit it means.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Sentence and Figure 1 chart labels (70, 34, 5, 2) read from page text and page image."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Gives 5 relevant articles for 2 openings; 3 remain after excluding pre-opening articles."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"2 is a count of openings; the paper's own count of relevant articles is 5 (or 3 after excluding pre-opening articles)."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"2","source_id":"S1","unit":"distinct openings","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Numerator in 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)'","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"5","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles coded relevant","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Five relevant articles reported for the two openings (4 Homborsund, 1 Stod)","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Both are counts within the same 34-article pilot, but one counts events and the other counts articles. The share of articles concerning a completed opening is 5/34 = 14.7% (3/34 = 8.8% after excluding the two pre-opening Homborsund articles), versus the reported 2/34 = 5.9%.","observed_discrepancy":"The reported 'about 6 percent' article share uses distinct openings (2) as the numerator over articles (34). On the paper's article counts the share is about 9% to 15%.","possible_explanation":"The authors may intend an event-yield measure (distinct openings per article) and used 'articles' loosely.","suggested_correction":"State the unit (e.g., 'two distinct openings, reported in 5 of the 34 articles (15%)'), or define the intended yield. Apply the same fix to the Figure 1 caption's 'Only 2 of 70 search hits'."},"suggested_fix":"Restate the yield with matching units: either 'two openings from 34 articles' or an article-level share (5/34, or 3/34 if pre-opening articles are excluded). Say which definition is used and align the Figure 1 caption."},{"id":"NUM-002","category":"internal count inconsistency","finding_summary":"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 and Section 4.1 show the second coder coded the Stord article relevant.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)","text_quote":"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not","precision":"partial"},"claim_text":"The project in Stord was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 3 has one article coded Not relevant by the pilot coder and Relevant by the second coder; the second coder's relevant total is 4 versus the pilot coder's 3. Section 4.1 says the only disagreement is the Stord municipality article, and Section 4.2 says the same article is the pilot–LLM disagreement. The Stord article is therefore coded relevant by the second coder and by the LLM (2 of 3 runs). It is coded not relevant only by the pilot coder. Footnote 3's statement that both human coders coded it not relevant conflicts with these counts. This affects the 96 and 44 totals, which rely on the LLM-relevant pilot articles.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"footnote 3","text_quote":"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"The quote continues 'relevant by both human coders (Section 4)' on the next line."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text (Table 3 and Section 4.1)","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1","text_quote":"Not relevant 1 30 31","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Row 'Not relevant' (pilot coder) shows 1 article coded Relevant by the second coder; column total Relevant = 4. The Stord disagreement is described in the following paragraph. Read from the page text, not the mis-columned table_3.md, per parser guidance."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Stord article coded not relevant by both human coders","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"Table 3 shows one article the second coder coded relevant and the pilot coder did not; Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord article."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"2","source_id":"S1","unit":"human coders coding the Stord article not relevant","sample":"Stord article, pilot, 2 human coders","denominator":"2 human coders","context":"Footnote 3: 'coded as not relevant by both human coders'","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"1","source_id":"S2","unit":"human coders coding the Stord article not relevant","sample":"Table 3, 34 pilot articles","denominator":"2 human coders","context":"Table 3 cell: pilot coder Not relevant, second coder Relevant = 1 article (the Stord article per Section 4.1)","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Same pilot article and the same two human coders; Table 3 and Section 4.1 define the disagreement article as the Stord article.","observed_discrepancy":"Footnote 3 implies 2 of 2 human coders coded it not relevant. Table 3 implies 1 of 2 (the second coder coded it relevant).","possible_explanation":"The footnote may be stale from an earlier coding round, or may refer to a stricter 'opening' definition that differs from Table 3's relevance coding.","suggested_correction":"Reconcile the footnote with Table 3, e.g. 'coded not relevant by the pilot coder'. If a different definition is meant, state it."},"suggested_fix":"Correct footnote 3 or Table 3/Section 4.1 so they agree on how each human coder coded the Stord article, and confirm how this article enters the 96 articles and 44 projects."},{"id":"NUM-003","category":"timing / period inconsistency","finding_summary":"The text says only the first quarter of 2024 is missing from the listings, but the Appendix and Figure 3 caption say the gap covers January to April 2024, which also touches Q2 2024; Figure 3 plots Q2 2024.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 Analysis / Figure 3","text_quote":"The first quarter of 2024 is","precision":"partial"},"claim_text":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Appendix A.1 and the Figure 3 caption state that listings from January to April 2024 are missing, which is 4 months. Figure 3 shows no point for Q1 2024 but plots a Q2 2024 point (about 39%) between the 2023 Q4 and 2025 points. April is part of Q2, so the Q2 2024 share would rest on at most two months (May–June) of listings, while the other quarterly points use three months. The text does not say whether Q2 2024 was computed on partial data or excluded, and the 'first quarter only' statement understates the gap.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 16 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2","text_quote":"missing listing text from January to April 2024.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"The figure caption gives the four-month gap. The statement 'The first quarter of 2024 is missing' is in the preceding body paragraph on the same page."},{"id":"S2","type":"figure","label":"figure_3.png","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_3.png","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2","text_quote":null,"url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-22f18338a427285653860df1","correspondence":"visual","verification_note":"Viewed the crop: points end at Q4 2023 and resume at about Q2 2024. A Q2 2024 point is plotted at about 39%. Point positions were read by eye and are approximate."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Only Q1 2024 is missing","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"The caption gap (Jan–Apr) extends one month into Q2 2024, which is plotted."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"4","source_id":"S1","unit":"months missing","sample":"Listing text data, 2024","denominator":"12 months in 2024","context":"Gap stated as January to April 2024","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"3","source_id":"S1","unit":"months missing (one quarter)","sample":"Listing text data, 2024","denominator":"12 months in 2024","context":"'The first quarter of 2024 is missing' implies January to March","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Same data gap described in the same appendix section and figure. Four months of missing data cannot be confined to one three-month quarter.","observed_discrepancy":"4 missing months versus 3 months in a single quarter, leaving April 2024 unaccounted for in the Q2 2024 point.","possible_explanation":"The Q2 2024 point may be computed from May–June only, or the April gap may be partial.","suggested_correction":"State whether Q2 2024 is based on partial-quarter data, and align the text with the January–April gap."},"suggested_fix":"Describe the gap as January–April 2024 consistently. Say how the Q2 2024 point was computed, or drop it if it rests on partial-quarter data."},{"id":"NUM-004","category":"classification rule vs reported shares","finding_summary":"The Table 9 rule 'first type in the table' puts 'bysykkelstativ' in Parking & storage (it contains 'stativ'), but the same paragraph counts it as infrastructure, so the Table 8 and Figure 2 category shares for that word are ambiguous.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions","text_quote":"given the first type in the table.","precision":"partial"},"claim_text":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing “bysykkel” (city bike), such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"In Table 9, Parking & storage appears before Infrastructure and contains the word part 'stativ' (rack). Infrastructure contains 'bysykkel'. 'bysykkelstativ' contains both parts, so the stated first-in-table rule gives Parking & storage, whereas the text says Infrastructure. Similarly, 'syklende' contains 'sykle' (Proximity, listed earlier) but is listed under Infrastructure. Figure 2 shows bysykkelstativ at 0.5% and syklende at 0.3% of all listings, and Table 8 category totals (Parking & storage 10.8%, Infrastructure 13.4%, Proximity 10.7%) depend on this assignment. The category on which the Table 8 counts rest cannot be determined from the text. This is a definition conflict, not a verified miscount.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 18 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2","text_quote":"given the first type in the table.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"The example about 'bysykkelstativ' follows in the same paragraph. The Table 9 rows were read from the page text, not the single-column table_9.md."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 16 text (Figure 2)","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 2","text_quote":"bysykkelstativ (city bike station) 0.5%","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Figure 2 bar labels read from page text."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"First-type-in-table rule assigns bysykkelstativ to infrastructure","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"By table order the word would be Parking & storage."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Which category (Parking & storage or Infrastructure) were 'bysykkelstativ' (0.5% of listings) and 'syklende' (0.3%) counted in when producing Table 8's 10.8% and 13.4%?","quantities":[{"value":"0.5","source_id":"S2","unit":"percent of all listings","sample":"700,579 FINN.no listings, Jan 2020 to Oct 2026","denominator":"700,579 listings","context":"Figure 2 share of listings containing 'bysykkelstativ'","rounding_half_width":"0.05","scale":"percent"}],"missing_information":["Which classification order was actually implemented","Word-level counts by assigned category","The overlap between listings containing these words and other words in each category, since the type shares are unions of listings"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"Reconcile the stated order rule with the stated example (and with 'syklende'). Report which assignment was used, and, if the rule was misdescribed, confirm that Table 8 and Figure 2 reflect the implemented classification."},{"id":"NUM-005","category":"additivity of totals","finding_summary":"The 96 article records and 44 projects are described as 92 + 4 and 43 + 1. The retained text does not establish that the pilot and the rounds 2–4 article sets are disjoint, or that the pilot's Homborsund and Stod projects are already among the 43.","issue_type":"cannot_verify","severity":"low","confidence":"low","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)","text_quote":"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.","precision":"partial"},"claim_text":"The 96 article records comprise 92 articles from rounds 2–4 and four from the pilot, giving 44 unique projects (43 plus Stord).","assessment":"cannot_verify","cannot_verify_reason":"The additivity of 92 + 4 and 43 + 1 depends on whether the pilot articles (searched 2 September to 10 October 2026) overlap with the 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4 (published October 2025 to October 2026), and whether the Homborsund and Stod projects are among the 43. The retained text does not say.","evidence_summary":"Section 5 gives 92 relevant articles and 43 projects from rounds 2–4, published October 2025 to October 2026. The pilot window (2 September to 10 October 2026) lies inside that period, and the pilot's four LLM-relevant articles (Table 4: 3 + 1) cover Homborsund, Stod and Stord. Footnote 3 treats only Stord as new, which implies Homborsund and Stod are in the 43 through rounds 2–4 articles. If any pilot article is also among the 3,187 articles, 96 double-counts it. The text does not state whether the rounds are disjoint, and Table 7 reports on 'rounds 1–4'.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"footnote 3","text_quote":"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote text on page 10."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 8 text (Table 4)","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md","page":8,"page_label":"8","section":"4.2","text_quote":"The only article they disagree on is the same","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 4 column total of 4 LLM-relevant articles is on this page. Used only to identify the pilot's four LLM-relevant articles."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"96 = 92 + 4 and 44 = 43 + 1","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"cannot_verify","note":"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 articles and projects is not documented."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Are the 4 pilot LLM-relevant articles disjoint from the 92 round 2–4 articles, and are the Homborsund and Stod projects among the 43 projects?","quantities":[{"value":"92","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"Rounds 2–4, 3,187 articles","denominator":"3,187 articles","context":"Relevant articles in rounds 2–4","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"missing_information":["Whether rounds 2–4 exclude the pilot's articles","Project-level overlap between the pilot and the 43 projects","Round definitions (round 1 = pilot?)"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"State that the rounds are disjoint at article level, or give the de-duplicated count. Say how the pilot's Homborsund and Stod projects map into the 43 projects."}],"notes":["Table CSV/markdown objects were not used as primary evidence, following the parser-quality guidance; table values were read from page text. The Figure 1 chart was read from the page-4 image and text.","Checked and consistent: 70 − 36 duplicates = 34; 34/70 = 48.6% (printed 49%); 5/34 = 14.7% (printed 15%); 5 + 8 + 21 = 34; 6 unclear for too little text + 2 planned = 8; Table 3 and Table 4 margins and 33/34 = 97.1%; 1/34 = 2.9% (printed 3%); Table 6 day 19 + month 10 = 29 and 19 + 10 + 9 + 5 = 43; 14 of 15 counties; ceremony split 18 + 26 = 44 and 17 + 2 = 19 day-dated; Table 8 sums and every share to one decimal (the 9.8% for 'bicycle' is 9.845%); Table 8 type counts exceed 'Any mention' (346,827 vs 266,625), as the table note allows; text county shares in Figure 4 (61, 52, 14, 13, 7) and the 38.1% national share; Figure 3 trend of about 35% to about 44% is about 9 percentage points as stated.","Table 5 road-link lengths (m0–1492 and m0–641) sum to 2,133 m against the reported 2,132 m; this is within rounding of integer reference positions and was not reported. The Geometry registered 4 September vs opening 5 October interval matches 'one month before'.","The statement that between a third and a half of projects contain most of the other Table 7 groups was checked: 6 of 9 groups fall between 33% and 50% of 44 projects (15/44 to 21/44), and Reasons for delay is 4/44 = 9%. The sentence is hedged with 'most', so it was not reported.","External figures (Copenhagen 60 percent, 5 percentage points for the Bergen tunnel, 96 percent accuracy in Bartik et al.) were not verified; they are literature claims outside this role's retained evidence.","No standard errors, regressions or effect sizes appear. Equations (1) and (2) are proposed specifications and contain no numerical results to audit."],"completion":{"version":1,"state":"complete","scope_description":"Numerical audit of work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed: all counts, percentages, shares, totals and dates in the main text, Tables 1–9 and Figures 1–4, with appendix definitions read before recomputation.","checks_completed":["Read the parser-quality guidance and used page text and images instead of mis-columned table CSV/markdown","Read the full text of all 18 pages and the main numeric claims in the abstract, introduction, results, conclusion and appendix","Recomputed the pilot funnel, retention percentages, duplicate counts and the 5 + 8 + 21 coding split","Recomputed the Table 3 and Table 4 margins, agreement percentages and 3% internal-consistency rate","Tested adding-up identities: Table 6 precision categories, 44 projects split by ceremony, Table 8 any/no mention total, and the non-additivity of type rows (stated in the table note)","Recomputed every Table 8 share against the 700,579 denominator and compared it with the Figure 2, Figure 3 and Figure 4 values and the text","Checked the percentage-point statement (35% to 44% = 9 points) against Figure 3, and the Figure 4 county shares and dashed national line against the text","Checked the Table 5 NVDB linkage numbers, the date interval and the road-link length sum","Cross-checked the Table 2/Table 7 counts and the 96 and 44 totals against Section 5 and the footnotes","Checked denominators and units in the text's yield statements"],"missing_checks":[],"evidence_limitations":["The Figure 3 point values were read by eye from the image and are approximate.","The Table 8 type shares are unions of listings and the word-level overlaps are not given, so category sums could not be tested.","Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 articles, round definitions, and the implemented classification order are not documented in the retained text.","External literature numbers were not verified."]},"coverage":[{"item_id":"assigned_remit","source_object_ids":[],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Systematic pass over the main text, Tables 1–9, Figures 1–4 and the appendix: recomputed counts, percentages, percentage-point differences, adding-up identities and denominators; read the appendix definitions first; compared text claims with displays.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Five issues found (yield denominator, footnote 3 vs Table 3, the 2024 gap period, the Table 9 rule vs example, the 96/44 additivity); the remaining checked numbers reconcile. numbers_in_text.json was not read item by item; the numeric claims were read directly from full_text.md and the page text.","finding_ids":["NUM-001","NUM-002","NUM-003","NUM-004","NUM-005"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce","source_object_ids":["OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159c